# Dry-run publish gate phase 4: Package Manufacture — Kestrel Toolkit
# release-candidate case study. One domain FRAGMENT of the shared
# kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle domain: this phase's 3 actions chain
# verify-complete -> manufacture-step1-done -> manufacture-step2-done -> manufacture-complete,
# so the merged cycle plan can only reach this phase after Phase 3
# (Verification Ladder) completes. 8-constraint split: every
# precondition/effect/goal here is a 1-conjunct (and ...) — far inside
# PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 — and each action takes 1 parameter
# (PDDL8_MAX_PARAMS=8); the dry-run harness asserts these bounds
# mechanically for every fragment (reusing
# crate::bench::togaf::verify_eight_constraint_split verbatim).
#
# DRY-RUN-OVERCLAIM FENCE (this phase runs `cargo publish --dry-run`, so
# read this carefully): the middle action here is cargo-publish-dry-run-locked
# — its effect atom is manufacture-step2-done, NOT "published" and NOT
# "crates-io-uploaded". `cargo publish --dry-run --locked` packages and
# validates a crate WITHOUT uploading it to crates.io; that is the whole
# point of this gate. Neither `cargo-package-locked` nor
# `cargo-publish-dry-run-locked` mutates any external registry, and the
# per-publish-set-member evidence in
# packs/dry-run-publish-pack/templates/dry-run-publish-case-study.ttl.tmpl
# records exit 0 with NO crates.io upload for each crate explicitly. See
# packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl for the full fence disclosure.
#
# Public-ontology doctrine: the artifact node is a blank node; the phase is
# identified by its public SKOS notation. The only private predicate is
# the cng pipeline's ABI carrier ceng:pddlDomain (urn:chatman:engine#),
# disclosed in packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "DRY-RUN-MANUFACTURE" ;
    dcterms:description "Package Manufacture domain fragment of the kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle STRIPS domain; the middle action is cargo publish --dry-run (local packaging validation, never an upload)."@en ;
    ceng:pddlDomain """
(define (domain kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle)
  (:requirements :strips)
  (:predicates
    (verify-complete ?x)
    (manufacture-step1-done ?x)
    (manufacture-step2-done ?x)
    (manufacture-complete ?x))
  (:action cargo-package-locked
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (verify-complete ?x))
    :effect (and (manufacture-step1-done ?x)))
  (:action cargo-publish-dry-run-locked
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (manufacture-step1-done ?x))
    :effect (and (manufacture-step2-done ?x)))
  (:action confirm-publish-set-coverage
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (manufacture-step2-done ?x))
    :effect (and (manufacture-complete ?x))))
""" .
